%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rules_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c4ae92e5dae156342ab8e00e812fd1cf, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 19206813229056
    m_Localized: The battle
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337920
    m_Localized: 'Gwent is a card game for two players. Win two rounds out of three: a round goes to the side whose cards on the board add up to more.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337921
    m_Localized: Factions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337922
    m_Localized: Each deck belongs to one of five factions, with its own ability and cards; neutral cards fit any deck.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337923
    m_Localized: Hand cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337924
    m_Localized: You draw 10 cards and may redraw up to 2 of them before the first round. Nobody draws between rounds, so every card you play is one fewer for the rounds ahead; only spies, a few leaders and the Northern Realms ability bring more.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337925
    m_Localized: Your turn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337926
    m_Localized: 'Do one thing: play a card, use your leader''s ability, or pass. Playing a card ends your turn.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337927
    m_Localized: Combat rows
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337928
    m_Localized: Units go on the close combat, ranged or siege row, as shown on the card.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337929
    m_Localized: Special cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337930
    m_Localized: Weather, Commander's Horn, Decoy and Scorch, and your leader's ability, can turn a round around.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337931
    m_Localized: Passing
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337932
    m_Localized: 'Passing is final for the round: you play nothing more in it, while your opponent may go on playing. Once both sides have passed, the higher total wins the round. A side with no card and no leader ability it could use passes on its own, and a side that starts a round with no card sits it out.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337933
    m_Localized: Life
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337934
    m_Localized: Each side has two gems and loses one with each round it loses; a drawn round costs both (unless Nilfgaard plays). Lose both and the battle is lost. The winner of a round starts the next one, and the board is cleared in between.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337935
    m_Localized: Playing well
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337936
    m_Localized: Winning a round by a mile wastes cards. Letting a round go and keeping a strong hand for the other two is often the better play.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337937
    m_Localized: The board
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337938
    m_Localized: Each side has three rows; yours are the lower half of the table.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337939
    m_Localized: Rows
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337940
    m_Localized: Close combat, ranged and siege, from the middle of the table out. A unit goes on the row shown on its card.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337941
    m_Localized: Strength
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337942
    m_Localized: A unit's strength is the number in its corner. Each row's total is on its left, each side's total by its portrait, the side ahead in a laurel.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337943
    m_Localized: Agile
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337944
    m_Localized: An agile unit can go on the close combat or the ranged row.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337945
    m_Localized: Horn slot
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337946
    m_Localized: 'The slot at the left of each row takes one card: a Commander''s Horn, or Skellige''s Mardroeme.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337947
    m_Localized: Weather board
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337948
    m_Localized: Weather cards and Scorch are played on the weather board, at the left of the table. Weather affects both sides.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337949
    m_Localized: Whose turn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337950
    m_Localized: The panel of the side whose turn it is is edged with glowing gold lines; a side that has passed is greyed out.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337951
    m_Localized: Discard piles
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337952
    m_Localized: Cards that leave the board go to their owner's discard pile, next to the deck. Tap a pile to look through it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337953
    m_Localized: Cards that leave the board go to their owner's discard pile, next to the deck. Click a pile to look through it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337954
    m_Localized: Cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337955
    m_Localized: A deck has one leader, at least 22 unit cards and at most 10 special cards, and holds each card at most as many times as it exists.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337956
    m_Localized: Heroes
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337957
    m_Localized: 'The gold-framed units. Nothing changes them: no weather, horn, morale boost, scorch, decoy or medic. A hero can be in a deck only once.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337958
    m_Localized: Units
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337959
    m_Localized: Everything else on the rows. Most exist once; a few, such as the Blue Stripes Commando, several times.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337960
    m_Localized: Special cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337961
    m_Localized: 'Weather, Commander''s Horn, Decoy and Scorch: they shape the board instead of adding strength.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337962
    m_Localized: Leader
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337963
    m_Localized: 'One ability you can use once per battle: lift the leader card, and its crown glows; the crown uses it. The crown turns grey once used. A few leaders'' abilities are always in effect instead.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337964
    m_Localized: Abilities
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337965
    m_Localized: Shown by the icons on a unit card.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337966
    m_Localized: Spy
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337967
    m_Localized: Goes on your opponent's side (adding to their total) and you draw 2 cards from your deck.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337968
    m_Localized: Medic
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337969
    m_Localized: Brings a unit back from your discard pile and plays it at once (no heroes or special cards). A medic brought back heals again.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337970
    m_Localized: Muster
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337971
    m_Localized: Plays every card of the same family from your deck and your hand at once.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337972
    m_Localized: Tight bond
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337973
    m_Localized: 'Copies of this card on the same row multiply each other''s strength: two double it, three triple it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337974
    m_Localized: Morale boost
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337975
    m_Localized: Adds 1 to every other unit on its row.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337976
    m_Localized: Commander's horn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337977
    m_Localized: Doubles the other units on its row, unless the row already has a Commander's Horn.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337978
    m_Localized: Scorch
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337979
    m_Localized: 'Destroys your opponent''s strongest unit(s) on that row, if the row totals 10 or more. The Clan Dimun Pirate''s scorch is the Scorch card''s: the strongest unit(s) on the whole battlefield as he lands (never himself).'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337980
    m_Localized: Agile
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337981
    m_Localized: Close combat or ranged, your choice.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337982
    m_Localized: Berserker
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337983
    m_Localized: 'Skellige''s Berserkers turn into bears on a row with a Mardroeme (the special card in its horn slot, or Ermion on it), whether it came first or they did: the Berserker (4) into the Transformed Vildkaarl (14, morale boost), the Young Berserker (2) into the Transformed Young Vildkaarl (8, tight bond). The Berserker goes to your discard pile as it turns: a medic can bring it back, to turn again. The bear only exists on the board, and vanishes when it leaves it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337984
    m_Localized: Avenger
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337985
    m_Localized: 'The Cow and Skellige''s Kambi: killed by a scorch, they are avenged at once, the Bovine Defense Force (8) or Hemdall (11, a hero) taking the field in your close combat row. Discarded any other way (cleared at the end of a round, or from your hand by Destroyer of Worlds), the avenger joins your close combat row at the start of the next round; if the battle ends first, it never comes. A decoy taking them back to your hand calls nothing. The avengers only exist on the board: no decoy or medic brings them back, and they vanish when they leave it.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337986
    m_Localized: Special cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337987
    m_Localized: Weather lowers every non-hero unit of its rows to 1, on both sides.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337988
    m_Localized: Biting Frost
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337989
    m_Localized: Weather on both close combat rows.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337990
    m_Localized: Impenetrable Fog
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337991
    m_Localized: Weather on both ranged rows.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337992
    m_Localized: Torrential Rain
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337993
    m_Localized: Weather on both siege rows.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337994
    m_Localized: Skellige Storm
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337995
    m_Localized: Weather on both ranged and siege rows.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337996
    m_Localized: Clear Weather
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337997
    m_Localized: Removes all weather.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337998
    m_Localized: Commander's Horn
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880337999
    m_Localized: Doubles the strength of the units on a row of yours, one horn per row.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338000
    m_Localized: Decoy
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338001
    m_Localized: Takes the place of one of your units, which goes back to your hand to be played again (not a hero, nor a summoned card such as the Bovine Defense Force).
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338002
    m_Localized: Scorch
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338003
    m_Localized: Destroys the strongest unit(s) on the whole battlefield, yours included (not heroes).
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338004
    m_Localized: Mardroeme
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338005
    m_Localized: 'Skellige''s own: in a row''s horn slot, it turns that row''s Berserkers into bears.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338006
    m_Localized: Factions
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338007
    m_Localized: Every faction has its own ability, always in effect, and its leaders to choose from (Skellige's two came with Blood and Wine). Hold a finger on a leader to read its ability.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338008
    m_Localized: Every faction has its own ability, always in effect, and its leaders to choose from (Skellige's two came with Blood and Wine). Rest the pointer on a leader to read its ability.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338009
    m_Localized: Controls
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338010
    m_Localized: Everything is done with taps; hold a finger on a card to look at it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338011
    m_Localized: The mouse does everything, and so do the keys.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338012
    m_Localized: Play a card
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338013
    m_Localized: Tap it in your hand (it shows large on the right), then tap where it lights up.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338014
    m_Localized: Leader
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338015
    m_Localized: Tap your leader, then its glowing crown; tap the empty place to put it back. Hold a finger on the crown to see whether it can still be used.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338016
    m_Localized: Choose cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338017
    m_Localized: "In the redraw, and when a card is to be chosen: tap a card to bring it forward, tap it again to take it. Done keeps the rest of your hand; \xD7 gives a choice up."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338018
    m_Localized: Pass
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338019
    m_Localized: Hold the Hold to pass button.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338020
    m_Localized: Look
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338021
    m_Localized: Hold a finger on any card (on the board, in your hand, a leader) to see it large; tap a discard pile to look through it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338022
    m_Localized: Zoom
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338023
    m_Localized: 'Spread two fingers on the board to zoom in. Zoomed in, one finger moves the board, and the padlock under the menu button locks it: taps then do nothing, to look around safely. Double tap the table to zoom in there or back out; the magnifier zooms out too.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338024
    m_Localized: A side at a glance
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338025
    m_Localized: 'Tap a side''s band (its portrait, name, gems or score): its faction''s ability, its leader''s and whether it''s used, its cards in hand, deck and discard pile.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206880338026
    m_Localized: Chat
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532224
    m_Localized: 'In a LAN battle: tap your portrait for the quick lines, its badge for the chat.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532225
    m_Localized: Back
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532226
    m_Localized: 'The Android back button steps back one thing at a time: a window closes, a chosen card goes back, a choice is given up (asked first), the board zooms out; then the pause menu. On the main menu it asks to quit.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532227
    m_Localized: Pause
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532228
    m_Localized: 'The menu button: resume, the rules, settings, leave the battle. The ? beside it opens these rules.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532229
    m_Localized: Give up
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532230
    m_Localized: In your turn, hold a finger on your deck, then confirm. It counts as a loss.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532231
    m_Localized: Play a card
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532232
    m_Localized: 'Click it in your hand, then where it lights up (a red sign shows where it can''t go). Keys: Left and Right pick a card, Enter takes it, Up and Down choose its place, Enter plays it, Esc puts it back.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532233
    m_Localized: Leader
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532234
    m_Localized: 'Click your leader, then its glowing crown; click the empty place (or Esc) to put it back. Keys: X, then X or Enter.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532235
    m_Localized: Choose cards
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532236
    m_Localized: "In the redraw, and when a card is to be chosen: click a card to bring it forward, click it again (or Enter) to take it. Space or Done keeps the rest of your hand; \xD7 gives a choice up."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532237
    m_Localized: Pass
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532238
    m_Localized: Hold Space, or the Hold to pass button.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532239
    m_Localized: Look
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532240
    m_Localized: Hover a card to see it large; click a discard pile to look through it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532241
    m_Localized: A side at a glance
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532242
    m_Localized: 'Click a side''s band (its portrait, name, gems or score): its faction''s ability, its leader''s and whether it''s used, its cards in hand, deck and discard pile.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532243
    m_Localized: Chat
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532244
    m_Localized: 'In a LAN battle: E (or a click on your portrait) shows the quick lines, and 1 to 8 says one. T (or the portrait''s badge) opens the chat: what was said, a message to type, mute.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532245
    m_Localized: Back
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532246
    m_Localized: 'Esc steps back one thing at a time, everywhere: a window closes, a chosen card goes back, a choice is given up (asked first); then the pause menu. On the main menu it asks to quit (outside the browser).'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532247
    m_Localized: Pause
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532248
    m_Localized: 'Esc or the menu button: resume, the rules, settings, leave the battle. The ? beside it opens these rules.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532249
    m_Localized: Give up
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532250
    m_Localized: Click your deck when the cursor over it turns into a hand, then confirm. It counts as a loss.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532251
    m_Localized: Pinch
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19206884532252
    m_Localized: Back
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
